<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Oenophyta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">457 BCE</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-peloponnesian-war">First Peloponnesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Oenophyta was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> in 457 BCE, about two months after the Spartan victory at Tanagra. An Athenian army under Myronides defeated the Boeotians, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> then dominated Boeotia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocis">Phocis</a> and Opuntian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locris">Locris</a>, supporting friendly regimes in the Boeotian cities. Athenian control lasted until the defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-coronea-447-bc">Battle of Coronea</a> in 447 BCE.</p></div>
